## Context

[Incident review](/kb/incidents/4471-review) shows that identical subjects can hide different bugs, and different subjects can share a cause. The old triage page was reviewed in June 2024 and is stale under the kb's 180-day rule. Its live explorer already disagrees with its subject-only instructions.

## Decision proposed to the support desk

Supersede decision 0001's subject-only deduplication rule. Join each report to its tenant and inspect locale, form, channel, and the reproduced mechanism. Merge only when both reports have the same non-null cause. An unknown tenant or an unexplained symptom needs investigation. A subject match alone is insufficient, and a subject difference alone is insufficient to split reports.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences

Triage takes more evidence than matching subject strings, but each engineering ticket has one mechanism, a defensible count, and specific reproduction steps. Keep anomalies visible and keep received dates separate from merge dates. Leave accepted decision 0001 unchanged; record approval of this replacement separately.

